      "content": {
        "kind": "items",
        "items": [
          {
            "heading": "",
            "text": "A sports career as a player is open to very few people and ends early, so the sensible plan keeps education going, uses official pathways, avoids pay-for-selection trials and builds a backup in coaching, analysis, fitness or management from the start."
          },
          {
            "heading": "",
            "text": "Train seriously, but treat study and a backup skill as part of the plan, not as a failure."
          },
          {
            "heading": "",
            "text": "Check the official association for your sport and be careful with private trials that charge to select."
          }
        ]
      },
      "type": "proof",
      "title": "Course Fees and the 10 Percent Test"
